  "Question": "Square dot arrays: 1, 4, 9. The number after 9 is \\(9 + 7\\). What is \\(9 + 7\\)? Calculate: \\(9 + 7 = ?\\)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "16",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The next square number is 16.\n\nAlternative method 1: Make ten\n\nSince \\(9\\) needs \\(1\\) to reach \\(10\\), split \\(7\\) into \\(1+6\\). Then\n\\[\n9+7=(9+1)+6=10+6=16.\n\\]\nThe result is \\(16\\).",
